# Drawer Footer Actions

Apply to every **right-side or left-side drawer** in the web UI (`Drawer` from `components/shared/drawer.tsx`).

## Rules

1. **Primary actions in footer** — Save, Suggest, Apply, Display, pagination, and other main drawer actions must use the shared `Drawer` **`footer`** prop so they stay pinned below the scrollable body. Do not place them at the bottom of scrollable content.

2. **Close in header** — Close (X) stays in the **top-right header** only (same as dialogs). Do not put Close beside the footer action.

3. **Scrollable body** — Drawer `children` hold form fields, previews, tables, and other scrollable content only. When `footer` is set, `Drawer` wraps `children` in the scroll region automatically.

4. **Shared content components** — If a component renders an inline action button and is reused in a drawer plus a full page or dialog, add a prop (e.g. `showSuggestButton={false}`) so the drawer parent can hide the inline button and render it in `footer` instead.

## Implementation

- Prefer shared `Drawer` from `components/shared/drawer.tsx`.
- Pass primary actions via `footer={...}`; omit `footer` only when the drawer has no primary action (e.g. read-only detail with in-content controls).
- Match dialog footer semantics: header = title + Close; footer = main action(s) only.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Suggest scrolls away with the form
<Drawer title="Quick Add Experience" open={open} onClose={onClose}>
  <div className="overflow-y-auto p-4">
    <ExperienceFactFormFields onSuggest={onSuggest} />
  </div>
</Drawer>

// ✅ GOOD — Suggest pinned in drawer footer
<Drawer
  title="Quick Add Experience"
  open={open}
  onClose={onClose}
  footer={
    <button type="button" onClick={onSuggest}>
      Suggest
    </button>
  }
>
  <div className="p-4">
    <ExperienceFactFormFields onSuggest={onSuggest} showSuggestButton={false} />
  </div>
</Drawer>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Apply at end of long suggestion preview
<Drawer title="Suggestion" open={open} onClose={onClose}>
  <ExperienceSuggestionContent onApply={onApply} />
</Drawer>

// ✅ GOOD — Apply in footer; preview scrolls
<Drawer
  title="Suggestion"
  open={open}
  onClose={onClose}
  footer={
    <button type="button" onClick={onApply}>
      Apply
    </button>
  }
>
  <div className="p-4">
    <ExperienceSuggestionContent onApply={onApply} showApplyButton={false} />
  </div>
</Drawer>
```
